.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt UNAME 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm uname ,
.Nm sethostname ,
.Nm setdomainname ,
.Nm sysinfo
.Nd get system identity and statistics or set the host and domain names
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/utsname.h
.Ft int
.Fn uname "struct utsname *buf"
.In unistd.h
.Ft int
.Fn sethostname "const char *name" "size_t len"
.Ft int
.Fn setdomainname "const char *name" "size_t len"
.In sys/sysinfo.h
.Ft int
.Fn sysinfo "struct sysinfo *info"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn uname
writes the system identity to
.Fa buf .
The six fields are 65-byte arrays containing null-terminated strings:
.Bl -tag -width "domainname"
.It Va sysname
.Ql Rach2 .
.It Va nodename
The host name of the caller's UTS namespace, initially
.Ql rach2 .
.It Va release
.Ql 1.0.0 .
.It Va version
.Ql "Rach2 musl port" .
.It Va machine
.Ql i686 .
.It Va domainname
The domain name of the caller's UTS namespace, initially
.Ql (none) .
Musl exposes this field as
.Va domainname
with
.Dv _GNU_SOURCE
defined, and as
.Va __domainname
otherwise.
.El
.Pp
.Fn sethostname
copies
.Fa len
bytes from
.Fa name
and appends a null byte to set the host name of the caller's UTS
namespace, and
.Fn setdomainname
its domain name.
A caller privileged in the user namespace that owns the UTS namespace may
set them, as on Linux: in the first namespaces, a caller with effective
user ID 0.
The length must be from 0 through 64.
A length of 0 sets an empty name without reading
.Fa name .
The host name is returned in
.Fn uname Ns 's
.Va nodename
field and by musl's
.Fn gethostname .
A process made with
.Dv CLONE_NEWUTS ,
or that calls
.Xr unshare 2
with it, has a copy of its parent's names that it changes alone.
.Pp
.Fn sysinfo
writes the 64-byte i386 system statistics structure to
.Fa info .
It reports:
.Bl -tag -width "totalram, freeram"
.It Va uptime
Seconds since boot.
.It Va procs
The number of process records, including unreaped children.
.It Va totalram , freeram
Total managed and free physical RAM, from the frame counts, in bytes.
.It Va mem_unit
1.
.It Va loads
The load averages over one, five and fifteen minutes, with 16 bits of
fraction, as
.Pa /proc/loadavg
reports them; see
.Xr proc 5 .
.It Va bufferram
The pages the buffer cache holds, in bytes, which
.Pa /proc/meminfo
gives as
.Li Buffers .
.It Va sharedram , totalswap , freeswap , totalhigh , freehigh
Zero.
.El
.Pp
The i386 system call numbers are 122 for
.Fn uname ,
74 for
.Fn sethostname ,
121 for
.Fn setdomainname ,
and 116 for
.Fn sysinfo .
The pointer is passed in EBX; for
.Fn sethostname
and
.Fn setdomainname ,
ECX contains the length.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return 0 on success, or -1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
The kernel returns a negative error number on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/miscprobe.c
calls
.Fn sysinfo
and checks that
.Va procs
is at least 1 and
.Va mem_unit
is 1.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EINVAL]"
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The result of
.Fn uname
or
.Fn sysinfo
cannot be written to user memory, or
.Fn sethostname
or
.Fn setdomainname
cannot read the specified name bytes.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The length passed to
.Fn sethostname
or
.Fn setdomainname
is outside the range 0 through 64.
.It Bq Er EPERM
The caller is not privileged over its UTS namespace.
.El
